sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/physiology-q10> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Q10 temperature scaling: the ratio between two temperatures is Q10 raised to their difference over ten (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "For a rate scaled by a Q10 factor, the ratio between two temperatures is Q10 raised to their difference over ten, and the logarithm of that ratio is linear in temperature." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Favored.lean) as an extension of the neutral case of Kimura (1962) to non-opposing selection; no paper states it in this form." ;
    skos:notation "X(T2)/X(T1) = Q10^((T2-T1)/10)" ;
    skos:definition """theorem q10_ratio {X0 Q10 Tref T₁ T₂ : ℝ} (hX : X0 ≠ 0) (hQ : 0 < Q10) :
    q10Scale X0 Q10 Tref T₂ / q10Scale X0 Q10 Tref T₁ = Q10 ^ ((T₂ - T₁) / 10)"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.Physiology.q10Scale" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.Physiology.q10_ratio", "Delphi.Physiology.q10_log" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "Pure consequence of the definition: it says nothing about whether any rate follows a Q10 law, and nothing about a value of Q10. No candidate commits a Q10 yet, so no constraint uses it." ;

    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: That a rate follows a Q10 law at all, and a value of Q10: both are inputs. The project's conditions fix 25 C and no candidate commits a Q10, so no instance is evaluated. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Physiology.lean>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/physiology-q10> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/physiology-q10> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-physiology-q10> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-physiology-q10> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.Physiology.q10_ratio with zero sorry and standard axioms; it also rejected 1 deliberately broken variant(s) of this statement or its model" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.3 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Physiology.lean (66 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.Physiology.q10_ratio, Delphi.Physiology.q10_log: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T22:57:06.367Z): 1 deliberate change(s) to this statement or its model were each rejected by the compiler: [q10-exponent-undivided] Statement changed to raise Q10 to the whole temperature difference instead of the difference over ten, which is the definition of Q10 (a factor per 10 degrees). Rejected with 2 error(s): Physiology.lean:27:75: error: unsolved goals Controls: 17 of 17 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/physiology-q10> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: That a rate follows a Q10 law at all, and a value of Q10: both are inputs. The project's conditions fix 25 C and no candidate commits a Q10, so no instance is evaluated. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

